{"cuisine/nigerian-cuisine":{"t":"cuisine","r":"cuisine/nigerian-cuisine","n":"Nigerian cuisine","c":"#e46a3f","crumb":[["Africa","cuisines#africa"],["Cuisine"]],"sub":"National cuisine of Nigeria","intro":[["Nigerian cuisine consists of dishes or food items from the hundreds of Native African ethnic groups that comprise Nigeria. Like other West African cuisines, it uses spices and herbs with palm oil or groundnut oil to create deeply flavored sauces and soups."],["Nigerian feasts can be colourful and lavish, while aromatic market and roadside snacks cooked on barbecues or fried in oil are in abundance and varied."],["Tropical fruits such as watermelon, pineapple, coconut, banana, orange, papaya and mango are mostly consumed in Nigeria."],["Nigerian cuisine, like many West African cuisines, is known for being savoury and spicy."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"nigerian-cuisine"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nigerian_cuisine"}],"sections":[{"h":"Recipe sites","count":2,"rows":[{"name":"Kitchen Butterfly","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"kitchenbutterfly.com","note":"Long-running blog by Nigerian food writer and historian Ozoz Sokoh, with Nigerian and New Nigerian recipes.","url":"https://www.kitchenbutterfly.com/about-2","suggested":true,"kind":"blog"},{"name":"Sisi Yemmie","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"sisiyemmie.com","note":"Nigerian home cooking recipes and meal plans, paired with the SisiYemmieTV YouTube channel.","url":"https://sisiyemmie.com/","suggested":true,"kind":"blog"}]},{"h":"Cookbooks","count":2,"rows":[{"name":"My Everyday Lagos: Nigerian Cooking at Home and in the Diaspora","color":"#f0b340","shape":"book","sub":"Yewande Komolafe, 2023","note":"Nigerian home cooking adapted for kitchens abroad by a New York Times Cooking contributor.","url":"https://www.penguinrandomhouse.com/books/646506/my-everyday-lagos-by-yewande-komolafe/","suggested":true,"isbn":"9781984858931"},{"name":"Chop Chop: Cooking the Food of Nigeria","color":"#f0b340","shape":"book","sub":"Ozoz Sokoh, 2025","note":"Survey of Nigerian dishes and ingredients from the writer behind Kitchen Butterfly.","url":"https://www.hachette.co.uk/titles/ozoz-sokoh/chop-chop/9781648291890/","suggested":true,"isbn":"9781648291890"}]},{"h":"Dishes","count":8,"links":[["Edikang ikong","dish/edikang-ikong"],["Edo black soup","dish/edo-black-soup"],["Miyar zogale","dish/miyar-zogale"],["Moin moin","dish/moin-moin"],["Ofada rice","dish/ofada-rice"],["Palm nut soup","dish/palm-nut-soup"],["Sinasir","dish/sinasir"],["Suya","dish/suya"]]},{"h":"Key ingredients","links":[["Beef","ingredient/beef"],["Palm oil","ingredient/palm-oil"],["Crayfish","ingredient/crayfish"],["Chicken","ingredient/chicken"],["Fish","ingredient/fish"],["Chili pepper","ingredient/chili-pepper"],["Egg","ingredient/egg"],["Catharanthus roseus","ingredient/catharanthus-roseus"],["Peppercorn","ingredient/peppercorn"],["Pumpkin","ingredient/pumpkin"],["Waterleaf","ingredient/waterleaf"],["Palm fruit juice","ingredient/palm-fruit-juice"],["Peanut","ingredient/peanut"],["Tomato","ingredient/tomato"],["Black-eyed bean","ingredient/black-eyed-bean"],["Black-eyed pea","ingredient/black-eyed-pea"],["Honey bean","ingredient/honey-bean"],["Onion","ingredient/onion"],["Iru","ingredient/iru"],["Milk","ingredient/milk"],["Cayenne pepper","ingredient/cayenne-pepper"],["Goat","ingredient/goat"],["Ram","ingredient/ram"],["Shrimp","ingredient/shrimp"]],"note":"Most used across its dishes."}],"cont":"African cuisine","img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/thumb/4/45/Akara.jpg/500px-Akara.jpg","w":500,"h":375,"by":"Atimukoh","lic":"CC BY-SA 4.0","licUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Akara.jpg"}},"cuisine/paraguayan-cuisine":{"t":"cuisine","r":"cuisine/paraguayan-cuisine","n":"Paraguayan cuisine","c":"#94bd5c","crumb":[["The Americas","cuisines#the-americas"],["Cuisine"]],"sub":"National cuisine of Paraguay","intro":[["Paraguayan cuisine is the set of dishes and culinary techniques of Paraguay. It has a marked influence of the Guaraní people combined with the Spanish cuisine and other marked influences coming from the immigration received by bordering countries such as Italian cuisine and German cuisine. The city of Asunción is the epicenter of the distinctive gastronomy that extends in current Paraguay and its areas of influence, which is the reason why it is considered the \"mother of the gastronomy\" of the Río de la Plata. It is worth clarifying that in the Paraguayan society, the exchange of knowledge between mestizos, creoles and cario-guaraní people occurred before the Jesuit missions."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"paraguayan-cuisine"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Paraguayan_cuisine"}],"sections":[{"h":"Recipe sites","count":1,"rows":[{"name":"Camila Made: Top 15 Paraguayan Recipes","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"camilamade.com","note":"Paraguayan recipe roundup on a Latin American home cooking blog.","url":"https://camilamade.com/top-15-paraguayan-recipes/","suggested":true,"kind":"blog"}]},{"h":"Dishes","count":5,"links":[["Chipá","dish/chipa"],["Dulce de batata","dish/dulce-de-batata"],["Paraguay cheese","dish/paraguay-cheese"],["Piracaldo","dish/piracaldo"],["Sopa paraguaya","dish/sopa-paraguaya"]]},{"h":"Key ingredients","links":[["Milk","ingredient/milk"],["Egg","ingredient/egg"],["Cheese","ingredient/cheese"],["Onion","ingredient/onion"],["Cassava","ingredient/cassava"],["Lard","ingredient/lard"],["Anise","ingredient/anise"],["Sweet potato","ingredient/sweet-potato"],["Bell pepper","ingredient/bell-pepper"],["Tomato","ingredient/tomato"],["Cornmeal","ingredient/cornmeal"],["Maize flour","ingredient/maize-flour"],["Paraguay cheese","ingredient/paraguay-cheese"]],"note":"Most used across its dishes."},{"h":"Within Paraguayan cooking","count":1,"links":[["Cuisine of Asunción","cuisine/cuisine-of-asuncion"]]},{"h":"More from Paraguay","count":1,"links":[["Guaraní foodways","cuisine/guarani-foodways"]]}],"cont":"Cuisine of the Americas","img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/thumb/0/02/Ensalada_de_porotos_con_tortillas_paraguayas.png/500px-Ensalada_de_porotos_con_tortillas_paraguayas.png","w":500,"h":309,"by":"Overkill53","lic":"CC BY-SA 4.0","licUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ensalada_de_porotos_con_tortillas_paraguayas.png"}},"cuisine/yao-cuisine":{"t":"cuisine","r":"cuisine/yao-cuisine","n":"Yao cuisine","c":"#f0b340","crumb":[["Asia","cuisines#asia"],["Chinese cuisine","cuisine/chinese-cuisine"]],"sub":"Regional cuisine in China","intro":[],"src":null,"wiki":"Yao cuisine","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"yao-cuisine"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Yao_cuisine"}],"sections":[{"h":"Recipe sites","empty":"None yet","tryLinks":[["Chinese cuisine","cuisine/chinese-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Part of","links":[["Chinese cuisine","cuisine/chinese-cuisine"]]}],"cont":"Asian cuisine"},"ingredient/toast":{"t":"ingredient","r":"ingredient/toast","n":"Toast","c":"#c9b8dd","crumb":[["Ingredients","ingredients"]],"sub":"Ingredient in 3 dishes across 4 cuisines","intro":[["Toast is sliced bread that has been browned by radiant heat. The browning is the result of a Maillard reaction altering the flavor of the bread and making it crispier in texture. The firm surface is easier to spread toppings on and the warmth can help spreads such as butter reach their melting point. Toasting is a common method of making stale bread more palatable. Bread is commonly toasted using devices specifically designed for such, e.g., a toaster or a toaster oven. Toast may contain more acrylamide, caused by the browning process, which is suspected to be a carcinogen. However, claims that acrylamide in burnt food causes cancer have not been proven."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"ingredient-toast"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Toast_(food)"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's cooked with","count":4,"groups":[["American cuisine","cuisine/american-cuisine",[["Club sandwich","dish/club-sandwich"]]],["British cuisine","cuisine/british-cuisine",[["Melba toast","dish/melba-toast"]]],["French cuisine","cuisine/french-cuisine",[["Canapé","dish/canape"]]],["New Caledonian cuisine","cuisine/new-caledonian-cuisine",[["Canapé","dish/canape"]]]]},{"h":"Often cooked with","links":[["Butter","ingredient/butter"],["Cracker","ingredient/cracker"],["Paste","ingredient/paste"],["Puff pastry","ingredient/puff-pastry"],["Spread","ingredient/spread"],["Bacon","ingredient/bacon"],["Chicken","ingredient/chicken"],["Lettuce","ingredient/lettuce"],["Mayonnaise","ingredient/mayonnaise"],["Tomato","ingredient/tomato"],["Turkey as food","ingredient/turkey-as-food"],["Turkey meat","ingredient/turkey-meat"]]}],"img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/thumb/3/35/Toast-3.jpg/500px-Toast-3.jpg","w":500,"h":458,"by":"Rainer Z ...","lic":"CC BY-SA 3.0","licUrl":"http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0/","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Toast-3.jpg"}},"dish/edikang-ikong":{"t":"dish","r":"dish/edikang-ikong","n":"Edikang ikong","c":"#ede6da","crumb":[["Dishes","dishes"]],"sub":"Dish from Nigerian cuisine","dot":"#e46a3f","intro":[["Edikang ikong is a vegetable soup made with ikong ubong that originated among the Efik people of Cross River State and Ibibio people of Akwa Ibom State in Nigeria It is considered to be a delicacy among some Nigerians, and is sometimes served during occasions of importance. Edikang ikong is a nutritious soup and expensive to prepare, and has been described as being mostly eaten by rich people in Nigeria. Ingredients used in edikang ikong include beef and dried fish, bush meat, crayfish, shaki (cow tripe), kanda, pumpkin leaves, water leaves, ikong ubong, onion, periwinkle, palm oil, salt and pepper."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-edikang-ikong"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Edikang_ikong"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["Nigerian cuisine","cuisine/nigerian-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Ingredients","count":8,"links":[["Beef","ingredient/beef"],["Catharanthus roseus","ingredient/catharanthus-roseus"],["Crayfish","ingredient/crayfish"],["Fish","ingredient/fish"],["Palm oil","ingredient/palm-oil"],["Peppercorn","ingredient/peppercorn"],["Pumpkin","ingredient/pumpkin"],["Waterleaf","ingredient/waterleaf"]]},{"h":"Cook it","rows":[{"name":"Kitchen Butterfly","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"kitchenbutterfly.com","note":"Long-running blog by Nigerian food writer and historian Ozoz Sokoh, with Nigerian and New Nigerian recipes.","url":"https://www.kitchenbutterfly.com/about-2","suggested":true,"kind":"blog"},{"name":"Sisi Yemmie","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"sisiyemmie.com","note":"Nigerian home cooking recipes and meal plans, paired with the SisiYemmieTV YouTube channel.","url":"https://sisiyemmie.com/","suggested":true,"kind":"blog"}]},{"h":"More from Nigerian cuisine","links":[["Edo black soup","dish/edo-black-soup"],["Miyar zogale","dish/miyar-zogale"],["Moin moin","dish/moin-moin"],["Ofada rice","dish/ofada-rice"],["Palm nut soup","dish/palm-nut-soup"],["Sinasir","dish/sinasir"],["Suya","dish/suya"]]}],"img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/thumb/0/07/Edikang_ikong.jpg/500px-Edikang_ikong.jpg","w":500,"h":375,"by":"Aderiqueza","lic":"CC BY-SA 4.0","licUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Edikang_ikong.jpg"}},"dish/pan-meino":{"t":"dish","r":"dish/pan-meino","n":"Pan meino","c":"#ede6da","crumb":[["Dishes","dishes"]],"sub":"Dish from Lombard cuisine","dot":"#cf5f87","intro":[["Pan meino (or pan de mej in Lombard) is a typical Lombard dessert, especially widespread in the provinces of Milan, Monza, Lodi, Lecco, and Como."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-pan-meino"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pan_meino"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["Lombard cuisine","cuisine/lombard-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Cook it","rows":[{"name":"Great Italian Chefs: Abruzzese recipes","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"greatitalianchefs.com","note":"Collection of Lombard dishes from Italian chefs on an established recipe site.","url":"https://greatitalianchefs.com/collections/lombardian-recipes","suggested":true,"kind":"site"}]},{"h":"More from Lombard cuisine","links":[["Gremolata","dish/gremolata"]]}],"img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/thumb/1/1d/Meino.jpg/500px-Meino.jpg","w":500,"h":333,"by":"Alezack","lic":"Public domain","licUrl":"","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Meino.jpg"}},"dish/pecel-ayam":{"t":"dish","r":"dish/pecel-ayam","n":"Pecel ayam","c":"#ede6da","crumb":[["Dishes","dishes"]],"sub":"Dish from Indonesian cuisine","dot":"#f0b340","intro":[["Pecel ayam is a traditional chicken dish of the Kemiren Banyuwangi Osing tribe of East Java, Indonesia."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-pecel-ayam"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pecel_ayam"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["Indonesian cuisine","cuisine/indonesian-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Ingredients","count":3,"links":[["Chicken","ingredient/chicken"],["Grated coconut","ingredient/grated-coconut"],["Siling labuyo","ingredient/siling-labuyo"]]},{"h":"Cook it","rows":[{"name":"Daily Cooking Quest","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"dailycookingquest.com","note":"Indonesian home cook Anita's blog with a large archive of Indonesian recipes.","url":"https://dailycookingquest.com/cuisines/indonesian.html","suggested":true,"kind":"blog"}]},{"h":"More from Indonesian cuisine","links":[["Arem-arem","dish/arem-arem"],["Arsik","dish/arsik"],["Asam pedas","dish/asam-pedas"],["Ayam goreng","dish/ayam-goreng"],["Ayam goreng kalasan","dish/ayam-goreng-kalasan"],["Ayam panggang","dish/ayam-panggang"],["Ayam Taliwang","dish/ayam-taliwang"],["Bajigur","dish/bajigur"],["Bakakak hayam","dish/bakakak-hayam"],["Bakpia","dish/bakpia"],["Bakwan","dish/bakwan"],["Bekasang","dish/bekasang"],["Betutu","dish/betutu"],["Bika ambon","dish/bika-ambon"],["Binte biluhuta","dish/binte-biluhuta"],["Bir pletok","dish/bir-pletok"],["Bolu kukus","dish/bolu-kukus"],["Botok","dish/botok"],["Brem","dish/brem"],["Bubur kacang hijau","dish/bubur-kacang-hijau"],["Bubur ketan hitam","dish/bubur-ketan-hitam"],["Bubur pedas","dish/bubur-pedas"],["Buntil","dish/buntil"],["Burgo (food)","dish/burgo-food"],["Cendol","dish/cendol"],["Cenil","dish/cenil"],["Cilok","dish/cilok"],["Cimpa","dish/cimpa"],["Corn fritter","dish/corn-fritter"],["Coto makassar","dish/coto-makassar"],["Dadar gulung","dish/dadar-gulung"],["Dadiah","dish/dadiah"],["Dengke mas naniura","dish/dengke-mas-naniura"],["Empal gentong","dish/empal-gentong"],["Emping","dish/emping"],["Es buah","dish/es-buah"],["Es doger","dish/es-doger"],["Es goyobod","dish/es-goyobod"],["Gado-gado","dish/gado-gado"],["Geplak","dish/geplak"]]}]},"dish/prawn-cocktail-steak-and-black-forest-gateau":{"t":"dish","r":"dish/prawn-cocktail-steak-and-black-forest-gateau","n":"Prawn cocktail, steak and Black Forest gateau","c":"#ede6da","crumb":[["Dishes","dishes"]],"sub":"Dish from British cuisine","dot":"#cf5f87","intro":[["Prawn cocktail, steak garni with chips, and Black Forest gâteau was the most popular dinner menu in British restaurants in the 1980s, according to contemporary surveys by trade magazine Caterer and Hotelkeeper. It was associated with the Berni Inn chain, which popularised mass-market dining out after the end of food rationing in Britain following the Second World War. The Prawn Cocktail Years, by Simon Hopkinson and Lindsey Bareham, called this meal the Great British Meal Out."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-prawn-cocktail-steak-and-black-forest-gateau"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Prawn_cocktail%2C_steak_and_Black_Forest_gateau"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["British cuisine","cuisine/british-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Cook it","rows":[{"name":"Great British Chefs: traditional British recipes","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"greatbritishchefs.com","note":"UK chef-driven recipe site with a large section of classic British dishes.","url":"https://www.greatbritishchefs.com/features/our-most-popular-traditional-british-recipes","suggested":true,"kind":"site"}]},{"h":"More from British cuisine","links":[["Banbury cake","dish/banbury-cake"],["Battenberg cake","dish/battenberg-cake"],["Black pudding","dish/black-pudding"],["Bread sauce","dish/bread-sauce"],["Carpetbag steak","dish/carpetbag-steak"],["Chelsea bun","dish/chelsea-bun"],["Christmas pudding","dish/christmas-pudding"],["Cobbler (food)","dish/cobbler-food"],["Crumble","dish/crumble"],["Crumpet","dish/crumpet"],["Curry in the United Kingdom","dish/curry-in-the-united-kingdom"],["Digestive biscuit","dish/digestive-biscuit"],["Dundee cake","dish/dundee-cake"],["English muffin","dish/english-muffin"],["Flies' graveyard","dish/flies-graveyard"],["Flummery","dish/flummery"],["Fritter","dish/fritter"],["Garibaldi biscuit","dish/garibaldi-biscuit"],["Hot cross bun","dish/hot-cross-bun"],["Hovis biscuit","dish/hovis-biscuit"],["Jammie Dodgers","dish/jammie-dodgers"],["Melba toast","dish/melba-toast"],["Mince pie","dish/mince-pie"],["Phall","dish/phall"],["Pickled egg","dish/pickled-egg"],["Pie","dish/pie"],["Ploughman's lunch","dish/ploughman-s-lunch"],["Potted shrimps","dish/potted-shrimps"],["Rich tea","dish/rich-tea"],["Sausage roll","dish/sausage-roll"],["Scotch egg","dish/scotch-egg"],["Shepherd's pie","dish/shepherd-s-pie"],["Soldiers (food)","dish/soldiers-food"],["Spotted dick","dish/spotted-dick"],["Tea sandwich","dish/tea-sandwich"]]}],"img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/thumb/f/f8/Cocktail_1_bg_060702.jpg/500px-Cocktail_1_bg_060702.jpg","w":500,"h":375,"by":"see below.","lic":"Public domain","licUrl":"","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Cocktail_1_bg_060702.jpg"}},"dish/semla":{"t":"dish","r":"dish/semla","n":"Semla","c":"#ede6da","crumb":[["Dishes","dishes"]],"sub":"Dish found in 2 cuisines","dot":"#cf5f87","intro":[["A semla, laskiaispulla, Swedish eclair, fastlagsbulle,  fastelavnsbolle, vastlakukkel, or vēja kūkas is a traditional sweet roll made in various forms in Sweden, Finland, Estonia, Denmark, the Faroe Islands, Iceland, Norway, and Latvia, associated with Lent and especially Shrove Tuesday in most countries, Shrove Monday in Denmark, parts of southern Sweden, Iceland and Faroe Islands or Sunday of Fastelavn in Norway. In Sweden it is most commonly known as just semla, but is also known as fettisdagsbulle, lit. 'Fat Tuesday bun' or 'Shrove Tuesday bun'. In the southern parts of Sweden, as well as in Swedish-speaking Finland, it is known as fastlagsbulle (plural: fastlagsbullar; semla on the other hand means a plain wheat bun with butter, called bulle in Swedish). In Poland it is known as ptyś. In Estonia it is called vastlakukkel. In Norway and Denmark it is called fastelavn"]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-semla"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Semla"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["Finnish cuisine","cuisine/finnish-cuisine"],["Swedish cuisine","cuisine/swedish-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Ingredients","count":4,"links":[["Almond paste","ingredient/almond-paste"],["Jam","ingredient/jam"],["Wheat bread","ingredient/wheat-bread"],["Whipped cream","ingredient/whipped-cream"]]},{"h":"Cook it","rows":[{"name":"Scandicuisine: Swedish recipes","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"scandicuisine.com","note":"Traditional Swedish recipes from Cecilia, a cook from a Finnish-Swedish family on Åland.","url":"https://scandicuisine.com/category/swedish-recipes","suggested":true,"kind":"blog"}]},{"h":"More from Finnish cuisine","links":[["Blodpalt","dish/blodpalt"],["Cabbage roll","dish/cabbage-roll"],["Egg butter","dish/egg-butter"],["Glögg","dish/glogg"],["Joulutorttu","dish/joulutorttu"],["Kalakukko","dish/kalakukko"],["Karelian hot pot","dish/karelian-hot-pot"],["Kesäkeitto","dish/kesakeitto"],["Kringle","dish/kringle"],["Kuivaliha","dish/kuivaliha"],["Lanttulaatikko","dish/lanttulaatikko"],["Lohikeitto","dish/lohikeitto"],["Lörtsy","dish/lortsy"],["Smörgåstårta","dish/smorgastarta"],["Strong beer","dish/strong-beer"]]}],"img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/thumb/2/2b/SemlaFlickr.jpg/500px-SemlaFlickr.jpg","w":500,"h":333,"by":"Frugan","lic":"CC BY 2.0","licUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/2.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:SemlaFlickr.jpg"}},"dish/spanish-omelette":{"t":"dish","r":"dish/spanish-omelette","n":"Spanish omelette","c":"#ede6da","crumb":[["Dishes","dishes"]],"sub":"Dish from Spanish cuisine","dot":"#cf5f87","intro":[["A Spanish omelette or Spanish tortilla is an omelette made with eggs and potatoes, often including onions. It is often served at room temperature as a tapa. It is one of the most popular dishes in Spanish cuisine."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-spanish-omelette"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Spanish_omelette"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["Spanish cuisine","cuisine/spanish-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Ingredients","count":3,"links":[["Egg","ingredient/egg"],["Olive oil","ingredient/olive-oil"],["Potato","ingredient/potato"]]},{"h":"Cook it","rows":[{"name":"Spain on a Fork","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"spainonafork.com","note":"Albert Bevia's video channel and site of traditional and everyday Spanish recipes.","url":"https://spainonafork.com/welcome2/","suggested":true,"kind":"youtube"}]},{"h":"More from Spanish cuisine","links":[["Andrajos","dish/andrajos"],["Bolinhos de bacalhau","dish/bolinhos-de-bacalhau"],["Buñuelo","dish/bunuelo"],["Caldo galego","dish/caldo-galego"],["Chistorra","dish/chistorra"],["Churro","dish/churro"],["Cocido","dish/cocido"],["Cuajada","dish/cuajada"],["Embutido","dish/embutido"],["Gazpacho","dish/gazpacho"],["Hojuela","dish/hojuela"],["Jamón","dish/jamon"],["Migas","dish/migas"],["Mojo (sauce)","dish/mojo-sauce"],["Patatas a lo pobre","dish/patatas-a-lo-pobre"],["Patatas bravas","dish/patatas-bravas"],["Picatostes","dish/picatostes"],["Pincho","dish/pincho"],["Pottage","dish/pottage"],["Salchichón","dish/salchichon"],["Salmorejo","dish/salmorejo"],["Sobrassada","dish/sobrassada"],["Soldaditos de Pavía","dish/soldaditos-de-pavia"],["Sopa de gato","dish/sopa-de-gato"],["Spanish restaurant","dish/spanish-restaurant"],["Stuffed peppers","dish/stuffed-peppers"],["Tapas","dish/tapas"],["Turrón","dish/turron"]]}],"img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/thumb/c/c0/Tortilla_de_Patatas_%28Corte_transversal%29.jpg/500px-Tortilla_de_Patatas_%28Corte_transversal%29.jpg","w":500,"h":333,"by":"Tamorlan","lic":"CC BY-SA 3.0","licUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Tortilla_de_Patatas_(Corte_transversal).jpg"}}}